 class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif"><br></div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif"><br></div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif">Quedo atento a sus comentarios.</div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif"><br></div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif"><br></div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif">Saludos,</div></div><div class="gmail_default" style="font-family:verdana,sans-serif"><br></div><span class="gmail_signature_prefix">-- </span><br><div dir="ltr" class="gmail_signature" data-smartmail="gmail_signature"><div dir="ltr"><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height:normal"><img src="cid:ii_19f8a70d2f801" alt="" width="420" height="54"></p></div></div></div>\n\n','\n',char(10)),'destaperapido.cl','respondido','2026-07-22T15:44:23.000Z','2026-07-22 15:44:46',NULL,replace('Buenas, el valor es de 250mil cada baño aseo cada 2 a 3 días \n\nY las 2 duchas 100mil cada uno (valores neto) \n\nSi le interesa la cotización formal me avisa','\n',char(10)),'2026-07-22T17:56:20.912Z',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'7c7aa245ccff963604e1d33bf78633187c3f96ab5f07b1438cdd9ab120277984','s:solicitud de cotizacion baños y duchas quimicas / obra cz la florida|mbahamondes@constructoravector.cl',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "correos" ("id","message_id","de","para","asunto","cuerpo_texto","cuerpo_html","dominio","estado","recibido_en","creado_en","respuesta_borrador","respuesta_enviada","respondido_en","adjunto_nombre","adjunto_b64","notificado","ajuste_pedido","ajuste_enviar","confianza","motivo_revision","dedup_hash","thread_id","in_reply_to","referencias","leido","estado_previo","etiquetas","estado_prev_papelera") VALUES(468,'<0100019f8aae2b7e-5cadfa88-71cf-4760-8a7b-692796d436ed-000000@email.amazonses.com>','zeno@updates.resend.com','contacto@destaperapido.cl','Claude, Codex, and our GitHub partnership',replace('Hey, it''s Zeno.\n\nWe''ve been pushing a ton of agent experience improvements, like adding an official Claude Connector https://resend.com/changelog/claude-connector, Codex Plugin https://resend.com/changelog/codex-plugin, and Remote MCP server https://resend.com/changelog/remote-mcp-server. We also started a new partnership with GitHub https://resend.com/changelog/github-secret-scanner to keep you safe. Plus, our first-ever conference, Resend Forward https://resend.com/forward, is coming.\n\nQuick question:\n\n> What do you wish agents could do with Resend?\n\nJust hit reply. We read every answer.\n\n\n\n\n\nCLAUDE, CODEX, AND REMOTE MCP\n\nhttps://resend.com/changelog/remote-mcp-server\n\nWe launched our remote MCP server that works everywhere. As part of our MCP initiative, we also published an official Claude Connector https://resend.com/changelog/claude-connector and a Codex Plugin https://resend.com/changelog/codex-plugin. Use MCP with all your agents today.\n\n→ Read the changelog https://resend.com/changelog/remote-mcp-server\n\n\n\n\n\nNOW SUPPORTING OAUTH\n\nhttps://resend.com/changelog/oauth-support\n\nWe now support OAuth connections to the Resend API. Your app opens an authorization URL, the user approves it on Resend''s own consent screen, and you get scoped access tokens back. No API keys change hands, and users can revoke access at any time.\n\n→ Read the changelog https://resend.com/changelog/oauth-support\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT THE NEW DMARC MEANS FOR YOU\n\nhttps://resend.com/blog/the-new-dmarc-is-here\n\nAfter more than a decade of real-world use and several years of drafting, DMARC has a new specification. Here''s what changed, and what it means for your domain.\n\n→ View the guide https://resend.com/blog/the-new-dmarc-is-here\n\n\n\n\n\nOUR NEW GITHUB PARTNERSHIP\n\nhttps://resend.com/changelog/github-secret-scanner\n\nResend is now a GitHub secret scanning partner. When a Resend API key is exposed anywhere GitHub scans (public repositories, gists, issues, and more), GitHub notifies us the instant it appears and we revoke keys automatically. This protects your domain reputation in case there''s a leak.\n\n→ Read the guide https://resend.com/changelog/github-secret-scanner\n\n\n\n\n\nNEW VERCEL INTEGRATION\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GjiQ0ImKXQg\n\nSet up Resend inside Vercel''s Marketplace in just a couple of minutes, including provisioning a brand new Resend team, connecting a Vercel domain, and auto-deploying API keys to your project. No DNS wrangling, no copy-pasting env variables.\n\n→ Watch the video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GjiQ0ImKXQg\n\n\n\n\n\nMESSAGE IDS NOW INCLUDED IN SENT EMAILS\n\nhttps://resend.com/changelog/message-id-for-sent-emails\n\nWe now include message_id in all email webhooks and in the retrieve and list email endpoints. This has been one of our most requested features, and it unlocks new use cases without any new primitives.\n\n→ Read the changelog https://resend.com/changelog/message-id-for-sent-emails\n\n\n\n\n\nLENNY''S AGENTIC EMAIL WORKFLOW\n\nhttps://resend.com/customers/lennys-newsletter\n\nResend powers the email behind Lenny''s Data, which gives his subscribers all of his posts, podcast transcripts, and more in clean markdown, an MCP server, and a GitHub repo. He set up the entire flow using Claude Code.\n\n→ Read Lenny''s Story https://resend.com/customers/lennys-newsletter\n\n\n\n\n\nJOIN US FOR RESEND FORWARD\n\nhttps://resend.com/forward\n\nWe''re hosting a conference to gather builders who care about their craft. It takes place October 21, 2026 in San Francisco. Can''t wait to see you there.\n\n→ Attend Forward https://resend.com/forward\n\n\n\n\nHappy sending,\nZeno Rocha\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nYou are receiving this email as a user of Resend.\n\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\nYou can unsubscribe from this list https://unsubscribe.resend.com/?token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJjb250YWN0SWQiOiI4Yjg2NjI1Yi0wOWU1LTRkNWUtYjhiYy0zZDhjYzM4ZmY1OGUiLCJhdWRpZW5jZUlkIjoiMzViMWNmZjEtYzM4MS00ZDZmLTk5NGUtNDkwNGY4NTVmMmM3IiwiYnJvYWRjYXN0SWQiOiJlYWUwZjdhZC02M2YwLTQ1OGQtYWE4Yy1lZGU3YzA2M2Q5MzkiLCJ0ZWFtSWQiOiI0MGI0OGMwOS0xYmYxLTRkNjItYWYyOS03YzE2MTNkMmVkNzUiLCJleHAiOjE4MTYyNjc3NjB9.sYvIIGWD3d0OPU1H0NCuT1nYBORv3d525Y8gncL3mRw.\n\n2261 Market Street #5039\nSan Francisco, CA 94114\n','\n',char(10)),replace('<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd"><html dir="ltr" lang="en"><head><meta content="width=device-width" name="viewport"/><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting"/><meta content="IE=edge" http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible"/><meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting"/><meta content="telephone=no,address=no,email=no,date=no,url=no" name="format-detection"/><title>Remote MCP server, OAuth support, the new DMARC, and more</title><style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){li::marker{color:#c4c4c4}}</style></head><body dir="ltr" lang="en" style="background-color:#ffffff;margin:0;padding:0"><!--$--><!--html--><!--head--><div style="display:none;overflow:hidden;line-height:1px;opacity:0;max-height:0;max-width:0" data-skip-in-text="true">Remote MCP server, OAuth support, the new DMARC, and more<div> ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏